while (n > 0) {
    Console.WriteLine(a);
    int temp = a;
    a = b;
    b = temp + b;
    n--;
}","code_language":"csharp","highlight":"The Fibonacci sequence is a series of numbers in which each number is the sum of the two preceding numbers."},{"type":"summary","title":"Key Takeaways","image_keyword":null,"points":["Loops are a fundamental concept in programming that allows us to execute a block of code repeatedly.","While loops are a type of loop that continues to execute as long as a certain condition is true.","For loops are a type of loop that executes a block of code for a specified number of times.","Do-while loops are a type of loop that executes a block of code at least once before checking the condition."],"closing":"In this section, we have learned about the different types of loops, including while loops, for loops, and do-while loops. Loops are essential in programming as they help us to perform tasks that require repetition."}]}

